 - [20261023-203956-feature-wait-exponential-jitter](20261023-203956-feature-wait-exponential-jitter/EXPERIENCE.md) — **when** A tenacity task asks for two or more separate additions to one API, where each can be missing on its own (a new keyword plus a newly accepted type for existing arguments, or several new options on one strategy). A single combined test would fail on whichever missing part it hits first. **then** Keep the clause in `system.md` step 1 that asks for one regression test per requested part, each shown failing for its own reason before the fix. Make it say that a test using an existing argument with a new type must not also pass the new keyword, because then its red run proves only that the keyword is missing.
